# Sustainable Fashion Research Plan Revision Update Improvements<br>
<br>
## Abstract<br>
<br>
This revised research plan aims to improve sustainable fashion practices in Paris by addressing key challenges and opportunities. The plan includes a comprehensive review of existing literature, stakeholder engagement, and recommendations for policy changes.<br>
<br>
## Introduction<br>
<br>
Sustainable fashion is essential for reducing environmental impact and promoting social responsibility. However, the current fashion industry faces significant challenges in adopting sustainable practices.<br>
<br>
## Methodology<br>
<br>
1. Literature Review: A comprehensive review of existing research on sustainable fashion will be conducted.<br>
2. Stakeholder Engagement: Key stakeholders, including designers, manufacturers, retailers, and consumers, will be engaged through surveys and focus groups.<br>
3. Recommendations for Policy Changes: Based on the findings from the literature review and stakeholder engagement, recommendations for policy changes will be developed.<br>
<br>
## Expected Outcomes<br>
<br>
1. Improved understanding of sustainable fashion practices in Paris<br>
2. Increased adoption of sustainable fashion practices among designers, manufacturers, retailers, and consumers<br>
3. Development of effective policies to support sustainable fashion in Paris<br>
<br>
